|WKBDeath Avengement
|WKO---------------------------------------------------------------------

|YKODeath avengement is the process by which players use to avenge their
last death, and attempt to restore any lost experience.

This system allows a player that just recently died, and lost experience
in that death, to ask another player to avenge his/her death. The
avenged and avenger have a set timeframe from the time of the original
death to successfully find and avenge the player's death.

If successfully avenged, any lost experience is halved and shared be-
tween the avenged and avenging player.

Previously, it was impossible to restore any experience that was lost
from death, so with this new exception, comes a few rules to how the
system works:

  |BKB* |GKBFrom the time of death, the avenged has 30 real time minutes to
    find an avenger, and for that avenger to track and kill the target
    mob.

  |BKB* |GKBNeither the avengee or the avenger may log off during that time,
    else that avenge is forever lost.

  |BKB* |GKBAn avenged player can only have one avenger per death.

  |BKB* |GKBAn avenger can only attempt to avenge one player at a time.

  |BKB* |GKBIf the original killing mob is killed, the avengement is cancelled.
    In the case of PKs, if the killing player logs off, the avengement
    is cancelled.


|WKBSee also: |YKBaskavenge, avengeinfo
